  "question": {
    "text": "Let points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> lie on the parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>△</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is an equilateral triangle and normals at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> on this parabola meet at the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
